## Vercel Web Analytics Integration

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the HallsSports Next.js application.

### Changes Made

#### 1. Installed Dependencies
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 using npm
- Package added to `package.json` dependencies
- Updated `package-lock.json` with new dependency tree

#### 2. Modified Files
**src/app/layout.tsx:**
- Added import: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/next';`
- Added `<Analytics />` component before the closing `</body>` tag
- Follows Next.js App Router best practices per official Vercel documentation

### Implementation Details

This implementation follows the official Vercel Analytics Quickstart guide (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart) for Next.js App Router applications.

The Analytics component was placed at the end of the body tag to:
- Ensure it loads after all other content
- Minimize impact on page performance
- Follow Vercel's recommended placement

### Next Steps

To enable analytics tracking:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Navigate to the Analytics section in your Vercel dashboard
3. Click "Enable" to activate Web Analytics
4. After deployment, verify tracking by checking browser Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/view`

### Testing Performed

- ✅ ESLint check passed on modified layout.tsx file
- ✅ Package installed successfully with npm
- ✅ Lock files updated correctly
- ⚠️  Build completed with pre-existing TypeScript error in src/app/admin/verifier/page.tsx (unrelated to this change)

### Notes

- The project uses npm as the package manager (based on package-lock.json)
- No breaking changes introduced
- All existing functionality preserved
- Analytics will only track once deployed to Vercel and enabled in dashboard
